Well, things certainly are more dangerous there - you can't pray in
Gehennom, there are several kinds of nasties you don't see much
beforehand, you have the whole bleeding ulcer of Rodney to contend with,
Air can be a terrible slugfest, and Astral has good old Pestilence and a
variety of other joy.

Now you *can* be prepared for all this, making the actual danger of dying
low, but that demands that you aren't overconfident. If you are
overconfident, it's easier to slip up because of all these perils than it
is on the middle game cruise down to the Castle.
